  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pre-Feasibility WASH@Home Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scale - drinking water</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The WaSH@Home programme in Ethiopia is intended to support the Government of Ethiopia and its institutions  in reaching specific objectives set forward in the OWNP-II section 10.2.8 page 114. This will result in  immediate positive effects for the beneficiaries of this programme, i.e. the households and its  members: on their health, education, income, available time, purchasing power and comfort. The  programme seeks to create liquidity within microfinance institutions allowing households to borrow  for WASH products and services. For the EIB trajectory, it is essential that the plans are assessed in  an external pre-feasibility study.</narrative>
  </description>
